messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: The correct option is: A/B/C.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is blue. Bob is white. Charlie is green. Charlie is quiet. Charlie is round. Charlie is white. Erin is blue. Erin is cold. Erin is green. Gary is big. Gary is blue. Gary is cold. Gary is green. Gary is quiet. Gary is round. Gary is white. White things are cold. If something is blue then it is white. If something is cold then it is round. If something is green then it is quiet. All round, big things are green. If Bob is round then Bob is big. All white, quiet things are big. If something is big then it is cold. If something is blue and quiet then it is cold.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Bob is not quiet.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', 'The statement "Bob is not quiet" is true.Here\'s the step-by-step reasoning:.\n\n1.From the context, we know that if something is green then it is quiet.(Charlie is green, so Charlie is quiet.).\n2.We also know that if Bob is round then Bob is big.(Gary is round, so Gary is big.).\n3.Since Bob is round, we can conclude that Bob is big.\n4.From the context, we know that if something is big then it is cold.(Gary is big, so Gary is cold.).\n5.We also know that if something is blue and quiet then it is cold.(Charlie is blue and quiet, so Charlie is cold.Bob is quiet.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
